course: dictionary
lesson: 15478
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one to use. Streamlining is one of these words. Look at the clues around it before you decide what it means.
explain: «The school streamlined its homework rules so that each subject had one clear form.» The clues are simpler and clear. Here streamlining means making something simpler and more efficient, with nothing cut away.
explain: «The bank announced streamlining, and two branches will close.» In business, streamlining can be a polite way of saying that jobs or services are being cut. This softer word for something hard to hear is called a euphemism. Ask: is anyone losing something? If yes, the business meaning is likely.
explain: «The dolphin's streamlined body cut through the water.» This is a science meaning: a shape that moves easily through air or water. When you meet streamlining, swap in simpler, cutting jobs or easy-moving shape, and see which one makes sense.
fact: Streamlining means making something simpler and more efficient.
fact: In business, streamlining can mean cutting jobs or services. It is a euphemism: a softer way of saying something difficult.
fact: In science, streamlining means shaping something so it moves easily through air or water.
fact: Streamline is the verb. Streamlining is its -ing form, and it can also be used as a noun.
exercise: «The school streamlined its homework rules so that each subject had one clear form.» What does streamlined mean here? | Painted in bright colours | Made louder and longer | Hidden away in a cupboard | *Made simpler and more efficient
exercise: «The company announced streamlining, and forty workers lost their jobs.» What does streamlining most likely mean? | Painting the office walls | Giving everyone a pay rise | Holding a party in the office | *Cutting jobs
exercise: The engineer said the new boat needed a streamlined shape to move quickly through water. What does streamlined mean? | Heavy and slow | *Shaped to move easily through water | Covered in sparkly paint | Full of holes
test: Which sentence uses streamlining as a business word that means cutting jobs or services? | *«The bank announced streamlining, and two branches will close.» | «The team streamlined the packing process.» | «The bird's streamlined body dived into the sea.» | «We walked along a wide, flat path.»
test: «The swimmer's streamlined body cut through the water.» What does streamlined mean? | Made into a heavy weight | *Shaped to move easily through water | Painted blue | Covered in stones
exam: Ravi says streamlining always means making people happy. What is the best answer? | Yes, it always means making people happy | It always means painting something | It is a type of food | *Not always: it can mean making something simpler, shaping something to move easily, or cutting jobs
